    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-051. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **layout-tree-verified delta** — same category as ADR-050.\n\n## The verified delta\n\nEmpirical smoke test (14 cases, all pass):\n\n```\n100vh                          -> 800.0\n50vh                           -> 400.0\n100vw                          -> 1774.0\n50vw                           -> 887.0\n100vmin                        -> 800.0\n100vmax                        -> 1774.0\ncalc(100vh - 48px)             -> 752.0   (was 0)\ncalc(50vw + 50px)              -> 937.0   (was 0)\nmin(50vw, 800px)               -> 800.0   (was 0)\nmax(50vw, 800px)               -> 887.0   (was 0)\n100px / 2em / 1rem / 50%       -> unchanged\ncalc(50% + 10px)               -> 210.0   unchanged\ncalc(100vh - 48px) vh=0        -> -48.0   (mathematically correct)\n```\n\n**`calc(100vh - 48px)` resolves.** That's the sticky sidebar's `max-height` rule that ADR-050 surfaced as still-unresolved.\n\n## The critical discovery during implementation\n\n**`parse_operand` has its own inline unit classification** separate from `parse_length`. Adding viewport units to `parse_length` alone made direct `100vh` work, but `calc(100vh - 48px)` still returned 0. Both paths needed the fix.\n\nThis is now documented in ADR-013's Post-ADR-051 note: future unit additions must touch both paths.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero first-viewport PNG delta in production.** `render_pipeline.cpp` passes `viewport_height=0`. Every `vh`/`vw` rule in Wikipedia CSS resolves to 0, exactly as it did pre-ADR-051.\n\n**The value is empirical, not visual**:\n- `parse_length(\"calc(100vh - 48px)\", viewport_h=800)` returns 752 (was 0)\n- When GTK height threading lands (future ADR), the sticky sidebar's `max-height` gets a real value automatically — no ADR-051 code change needed\n- 18 unit tests with explicit viewport dims verify the correct resolution end-to-end\n\n## Remaining sticky prerequisites (all separate)\n\nFrom ADR-050's Post-ADR-051 note:\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `@supports (display: grid)` gate | ADR-050 unblocked |\n| `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)` | **ADR-051 resolves to a number** |\n| Layout reads `max-height` | Deferred (min/max clamp ADR) |\n| Ancestor culling | Deferred (separate culling rules) |\n| GTK height threading | Deferred (separate concern) |\n| `position: sticky` scroll-Y | Deferred (separate cycle) |\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-051 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-051 note in ADR-013 (units family table + parse_length/parse_operand sync discipline)\n- Post-ADR-051 note in ADR-050 (calc(100vh - ...) unblocked, remaining chain enumerated)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- 644 cases / 2465 assertions all pass\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #234\n",
